  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-10T05:11:45.005Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Every time I launch VRChat to hang out with friends, we always have to do the same sequence of events to first join up before we go world hopping. I feel like it could be super useful and convenient to have an option to conjoin your home room with another player, or group of players.\nEssentially, everyone who is in that group gets dumped into the same home room on game launch to skip multiple steps of having to meet up or coordinate with others externally from VRC. \nThis could create friend-group communal rooms that act as a hub for meeting up initially as well as if people are already in there waiting. This would be SO much better than having to request invite to all your friends and see who is available. Less guessing, more meeting! Instant join back to your home room with the \"go home\" button to see who's there without any invite needed or making a public / friends instance.",
